\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs36 \i\f1\fs36 Concerning the Catechism}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 This catechism is primarily intended for use by parish priests, deacons, and \softline
lay catechists, to give an outline for instruction. It is a commentary on the \softline
creeds, but is not meant to be a complete statement of belief and practice; \softline
rather, it is a point of departure for the teacher, and it is cast in the \softline
traditional question and answer form for ease of reference.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 The second use of this catechism is to provide a brief summary of the\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 Church's teaching for an inquiring stranger who picks up a Prayer Book.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 It may also be used to form a simple service; since the matter is arranged \softline
under headings, it is suitable for selective use, and the leader may introduce \softline
prayers and hymns as needed.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20  }{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
